orientation/config.local.json
config.local.json

# Python bytecode from the labeler helper scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# chin tuck 0.0/1.0 frames — untracked since the 2.0 rollout (GitHub Pages
# refuses to publish a site over 1 GB and these were 467 MB of it). That
# originally left chin_tuck.html/chin_tuck_john.html unable to load frames
# from Pages at all — fixed 2026-08 by moving the JPEGs to Firebase
# Storage (labeler_media/chin_tuck/v1/frames/, same bucket every
# v2/v3/v4 pool uses); chin_tuck.js / chin_tuck_john.js build Firebase
# URLs now, not a local path. Still ignored here because the JPEGs are a
# DERIVED artifact — cornerman-backend's chin_export_frames.py rebuilds
# them from the source videos in about an hour — so a local export copy
# should never get committed by accident. 0.0 has no frames/ of its own —
# it reads 1.0's pool, same as 3.0 reads 2.0's.
chin_tuck_1.0/frames/

